    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d129">

                <pb facs="0220" n="146" sameAs="frus:frus1866p1/pg146"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Mr.
                        Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1230.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-07-07"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 7, 1866</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have received a telegraphic despatch from
                    Mr. West, the consult Dublin, communicating the information that Colonel Burke
                    and Daniel <pb facs="0221" n="147" xml:id="pg147"/> Mykins had been liberated. I
                    regret to learn also that the reply in the ease of Hynes is very unfavorable.
                    Mr. West promises a full report in a despatch by the post on Monday. But as that
                    will be too late for the bag this week, I thought it best to communicate the
                    substance of his report to you at once.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
